00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:08.550
Microsoft Security
Copilot is an AI-powered,

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:13.140
cloud-based security analysis
tool that helps analysis

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:18.150
like us respond to threats
quickly, process signal

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:22.980
at machine speed, and
access risk, expose faster

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.620
than may otherwise be possible.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.800
In other words, it's
designed to help you move

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:34.530
from raw security data to
actionable understanding

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:38.490
without losing time
on manual synthesis.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:42.930
Security Copilot combines
powerful large language model

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.620
with security-specific
models from Microsoft.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:51.240
It integrates Microsoft
and non-Microsoft sources,

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:56.550
and it learns at machine speed
to help analysts identify

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:59.880
and respond to emerging threats.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:03.990
Just as importantly,
enterprise data is protected

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:08.400
by comprehensive enterprise
compliance and security control,

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.220
so you can apply AI assistance

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.940
without compromising
governance expectation.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:18.000
Now let's take a look

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.600
at the core use cases
of Security Copilot.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.060
It's designed to make easy.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:27.720
One common scenario is
incident summarization,

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.470
using generative AI to
distill complex alert

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.890
into concise,
actionable summaries.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:39.720
This helps you gain context
quickly and communicate clearly

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.040
across your organization, which
can lead to faster response

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:46.500
and better decision-making.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.200
Another scenario is
impact analysis,

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:55.230
where AI-driven analytics helps
you assess the potential impact

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:59.460
of an incident, highlighting
affected system and data

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.850
so you can prioritize
response efforts.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:06.510
A third scenario is reverse
engineering of scripts.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.630
Instead of manually
unpacking complex

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.480
or obfuscated
command-line scripts,

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:16.440
Copilot can translate the
script into natural language

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:20.370
and explain what action
are being performed,

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:24.750
while also helping you extract
and link indicator found

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:28.410
in the script to entities
in your environment.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:32.160
Finally, guided responses
provide step-by-step

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.530
recommendation for triage,
investigation, containment,

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:41.010
and remediation,
often with deep links

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:44.970
to help you take actions faster.

